                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I bought this game at launch. I even bought a switch copy of it that came with a Kawase keychain. I never really noticed the detail put into some of the characters until recently. Despite being a Solange main, I can't help but to enjoy the visual designs as well as the mechanics that a few of these characters have. More often then not when I try a certain character, I see what the devs were going for when creating each character. As someone who does like to play a little mind games, someone like Helen, Ali or Lina feel like great characters for me to main. Lina to me is my second favorite design wise as. Speaking of character design choices: Besides Lina being my favorite, my other favorites would have to be Curly, Shovel Knight as well as Piaa. The original characters made exclusively for this game are the type that inspire me to want to make characters based on them. \n\nI do like how simple this game feels and the ceiling is indeed very high based on my recollection of when this game was it's most active. The floaty feel is also something that did take a while for me to get used to as someone who plays fast paced anime fighting games so to me at the time was a breath of fresh air. I also recall this game declining very fast because of Curly and Shovel Knight being their absolute strongest on release. It's very unfortunate that no one else shined as much as those two during the first month of this game's release. I've not looked at the history behind the devs but a google search behind the devs shows to me that this is the first fighting game made under the company. whoever was behind it, i appreciate the effort went into making the game as balanced and as in-depth as they could. I am personally able to see it and while I myself am not very good at the game, the players I went against at the time really did sink their teeth into the game's mechanics.\n\nThe story...wasn't good...having a gallery of sorts in the game for people to see would have been nice as well. The music outside the bath house and training room did not sound as well to my ears. I did not have issues with the controls as someone who plays stick. My fond memories and bias towards this game makes it somewhat difficult to point out any other major flaws if any.\n\nAs I finish up this review, I realize this game is 8 years old now. I am old...this game is fun. I'm happy to have been able to play it at its peak at the time and while my review of it comes this late, it does hold a special place in my heart. Also it was released on my birthday lol. Solange is queen.",
